From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:40:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 042/110] Two views side by side: Move and Clone to other view

View, "Move to other view" and "Clone to other view" (also in the tab's
right-click menu) split the window into a left and a right view, each with
its own tab bar and shown tab. A view left without tabs closes the split.
A click into a view makes it active; menus, shortcuts and Ctrl+Tab act on
the active view, and Close all/others/to the right on the tab's view.

All tabs stay in the one tab model, so drafts, diffs and disk checks keyed
by tab work unchanged; each view has a display model pointing at them,
synced after every message (update now wraps update_message).

Clone opens the saved file again as a second tab (separate buffer); both
follow changes on disk. Unsaved and untitled tabs cannot be cloned.

"Synchronize vertical scrolling" (View, off by default, config
sync_scroll_views): scrolling one view scrolls the other by as many lines.

The session keeps each tab's view and the other view's shown tab (serde
defaults; older sessions load into one view).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

